@startuml UC-006-analysis-sequence
!include ../../../diagrams/style.iuml
title UC-006 Run complete evaluation: analysis sequence diagram

actor Developer
boundary "Command Line" as CLI
control "Run Evaluation" as Run
boundary "Config File" as CF
entity "Evaluation Run" as ER
entity "Case Result" as CR
boundary "Model Interface" as MI
actor "Target model" as TM
actor "Judge model" as JM
boundary "Report Store" as RS

Developer -> CLI : run(config file, output directory?)
opt 1c: no --config
  CLI --> Developer : usage message, exit code 2
end
CLI -> Run : run(config file, output directory?)
Run -> CF : read config
CF --> Run : evaluation config (profiles, dataset, rubric id, output)
Run -> Run : load benchmark, look up rubric,\nopen target and judge connections (UC-001, UC-002)
alt 1a: the setup is invalid (config, benchmark, rubric, connection, key)
  Run -> CLI : error
  CLI --> Developer : "error: ..." on stderr, exit code 1
  note right of CLI
    No model called, no report written,
    no traceback, no pasted key echoed.
  end note
else the setup is valid
  Run -> CLI : show benchmark, target, judge and rubric
  CLI --> Developer : benchmark name and size, target, judge and rubric
  Run -> ER : start(now)
  loop each test case, in order
    Run -> MI : ask the target the question (UC-003)
    MI -> TM : question
    TM --> MI : answer, refusal or error
    MI --> Run : answer, refusal or error
    opt 3a: the answer can be trusted (not failed, not cut off)
      Run -> MI : ask the judge for a verdict (UC-004),\na refusal marked [refused]
      MI -> JM : judge request
      JM --> MI : verdict, or error or unusable reply
      MI --> Run : verdict, or error
    end
    Run -> CR : create(case, outcome = verdict, evidence)
    Run -> CLI : show progress line (case evaluated)
    CLI --> Developer : progress line "[i/n] id: OUTCOME"
  end
  Run -> ER : finish(now)
  Run -> Run : summarise and build the report (UC-005)
  Run -> RS : write report
  RS --> Run : report path
  Run -> CLI : show totals, pass rate with coverage, report path
  CLI --> Developer : totals, pass rate with coverage,\nreport path, exit code 0
end

note right of MI
  Extensions 3a, 4a: a failed or cut-off answer is not judged;
  a judge failure is ERROR at the judge stage, never FAIL.
  An auth or quota failure stops the rest of that stage.
end note
@enduml
